(5624081, 814154, 54645, '<td valign="top">Well done Lydia, placed high despite the DNMC votes. Reading the comments it seems that the bird was too attractive and well captured! Interesting that the cat and fish took second.  I happen to really like that shot as well. When looking at that photograph the placement of the appliance was more visually prominent. In hindsight, taking the comments and other images into context, the flower is too dominant and immediately brings in the hummingbird, then, oh by the way the toaster. Although I can honestly say that I would have been on the 6 plus end if I voted, I think many of the 4 and under crowd were taken aback by the placement and prominence of the flower. It''s still creative, humorous, and fresh despite the hummingbird.</td>', 'Well done Lydia, placed high despite the DNMC votes. Reading the comments it seems that the bird was too attractive and well captured! Interesting that the cat and fish took second.  I happen to really like that shot as well. When looking at that photograph the placement of the appliance was more visually prominent. In hindsight, taking the comments and other images into context, the flower is too dominant and immediately brings in the hummingbird, then, oh by the way the toaster. Although I can honestly say that I would have been on the 6 plus end if I voted, I think many of the 4 and under crowd were taken aback by the placement and prominence of the flower. It''s still creative, humorous, and fresh despite the hummingbird.', '2009-08-26 01:29:13.000000', NULL, 0),
