(5625396, 814154, 46918, '<td valign="top">I really liked this pic. I was one of your "8" votes. I think you should have done better that 15th place. However it''s not bad...Good job</td>', 'I really liked this pic. I was one of your "8" votes. I think you should have done better that 15th place. However it''s not bad...Good job', '2009-08-26 19:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625397, 813642, 55330, '<td valign="top">I got the same Microwave</td>', 'I got the same Microwave', '2009-08-26 19:28:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625695, 814820, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for an in depth comment on your recent photograph in this challenge. I gave you a 6 in this challenge and these are some of the reasons why, <br/> <br/>The lighting is fairly hash in this and the reflections are hard light. A different crop, ie closer to the subject would have helped this as well , because as of right now it is just sort of sitting in mid air.  Your clarity is spot on , you are sharp in all the right places. <br/> <br/>I do not think that there is much that you could do in post processing.  I think this could have been all done in the set up of the shot. Do not be afraid to try different or odd angles, throw something into the mixer like flour and see what happens. <br/> <br/>Over all a good product shot though</td>', 'Hi from the C Club You asked for an in depth comment on your recent photograph in this challenge. I gave you a 6 in this challenge and these are some of the reasons why,  The lighting is fairly hash in this and the reflections are hard light. A different crop, ie closer to the subject would have helped this as well , because as of right now it is just sort of sitting in mid air.  Your clarity is spot on , you are sharp in all the right places.  I do not think that there is much that you could do in post processing.  I think this could have been all done in the set up of the shot. Do not be afraid to try different or odd angles, throw something into the mixer like flour and see what happens.  Over all a good product shot though', '2009-08-26 23:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625704, 814163, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club<br/> <br/>You asked for an in depth comment on your recent photograph in this challenge. <br/> <br/>Nice shot of appliances here. <br/> <br/>I think that I am one of those ones that didn''t really feel your reflections so much. I saw the oven, then all I saw and what kept drawing my eye was the electrical plug and wall.  Repositioning   the toaster could have eliminated this . having the toaster on the edge of the counter would have given you the whole reflection of the oven versus it just being cut off in the middle of the toaster and leaving dead space there, <br/> <br/>Your ISO is way up there and accounts for the grain that I am seeing also, try a faster shutter speed or more light. The reflection of the power cord is a little distracting and could have been laid more flat and even mroe in focus. <br/> <br/>Your POV is great, your DOF is good also, overall this is a good clean shot of an appliance, well done</td>', 'Hi from the C Club You asked for an in depth comment on your recent photograph in this challenge.  Nice shot of appliances here.  I think that I am one of those ones that didn''t really feel your reflections so much. I saw the oven, then all I saw and what kept drawing my eye was the electrical plug and wall.  Repositioning   the toaster could have eliminated this . having the toaster on the edge of the counter would have given you the whole reflection of the oven versus it just being cut off in the middle of the toaster and leaving dead space there,  Your ISO is way up there and accounts for the grain that I am seeing also, try a faster shutter speed or more light. The reflection of the power cord is a little distracting and could have been laid more flat and even mroe in focus.  Your POV is great, your DOF is good also, overall this is a good clean shot of an appliance, well done', '2009-08-27 00:03:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5625833, 814561, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to DPC.  People around here shoot for all different reasons.  Some shoot for scores, some shoot to share their work, some start here and move on to greater things.  Whatever your reasons for signing up were, welcome.  I hope you decide to stick around and shoot more.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> I do see your primary are of focus here, and I can appreciate the reflection of the various colors bleeding into one.  I can also see how other users and voters could believe that those technical aspects were off, as well.  I think your title explains the intention of the technicals.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I like the lighting in your image.  In fact, I think that it is the single strength that adds interest and depth.  It is a bit of an abstraction, at least somewhat.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Content...I am neutral.  The image does depict kitchen instruments.  Composition...feels very uncomfortable.  Leaving empty space at the top and chopping the tools off at the bottom of the frame gives more of an accidental feeling to the composition than one of intention.  I think the composition is perhaps the largest perceived weakness of the capture.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> 4.02 is a starting place at least.  I cannot say that I disagree with the voters on this one, but entry into challenges alone is worth merit.  I would have scored it in the 4 to 5 range, so I think the voters hot the mark with this one.  Now you have your first entry in, and you see how voters cast their numbers.  Again, it all depends on why you shoot.  Do you shoot for the scores or for capturing images you like?  Welcome.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, welcome to DPC.  People around here shoot for all different reasons.  Some shoot for scores, some shoot to share their work, some start here and move on to greater things.  Whatever your reasons for signing up were, welcome.  I hope you decide to stick around and shoot more. Camera Work/Technical: I do see your primary are of focus here, and I can appreciate the reflection of the various colors bleeding into one.  I can also see how other users and voters could believe that those technical aspects were off, as well.  I think your title explains the intention of the technicals. Lighting: I like the lighting in your image.  In fact, I think that it is the single strength that adds interest and depth.  It is a bit of an abstraction, at least somewhat. Composition/Content: Content...I am neutral.  The image does depict kitchen instruments.  Composition...feels very uncomfortable.  Leaving empty space at the top and chopping the tools off at the bottom of the frame gives more of an accidental feeling to the composition than one of intention.  I think the composition is perhaps the largest perceived weakness of the capture. My Opinion: 4.02 is a starting place at least.  I cannot say that I disagree with the voters on this one, but entry into challenges alone is worth merit.  I would have scored it in the 4 to 5 range, so I think the voters hot the mark with this one.  Now you have your first entry in, and you see how voters cast their numbers.  Again, it all depends on why you shoot.  Do you shoot for the scores or for capturing images you like?  Welcome. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-08-27 03:09:27.000000', NULL, 0),
